Q7 – Design a Contact-Merging Program from First Principles (10 Marks)
1. Requirements and identity rule
Input: contact records from two phones and a SIM, each potentially containing a name, phone number and email. Output: merged
contacts, with one group per normalised phone number and sets of all known names, phone formats and email addresses.
Identity rule: records are treated as the same person when they share a normalised phone number. A matching name alone is not
enough because different people can share a name. Measurable requirements: normalise phone digits consistently; merge duplicate
numbers; preserve all non-empty emails and names; handle missing fields; produce one output record per normalised phone key.
2. Normalisation and pseudocode
def normalise_phone(phone):
    if not phone:
        return ""
    digits = "".join(ch for ch in phone if ch.isdigit())
    # For this India-focused example, remove leading country code 91
    # only when the number contains 12 digits.
    if len(digits) == 12 and digits.startswith("91"):
        digits = digits[2:]
    return digits
